## Analysis summary

The job: allow users to rename todo categories from the settings → todos section, using `PUT /api/v1/todos/categories/{category}` with `title` in the body.

Current state of the code:
- `apiRoutes.todos` has `listCategories`, `createCategory`, `deleteCategory` — **no** `updateCategory` route (notes, links, and time-tracking all have one, so the pattern is well established).
- `Todos.svelte.ts` has `createCategory`/`deleteCategory` but no `updateCategory` method.
- `CategoryEdit.svelte` (used only by `TodoSettings.svelte`) renders `/{category.title}` plus a delete button — no edit affordance.
- `todo.ts` has `CreateTodoCategoryRequest` but no `UpdateTodoCategoryRequest`.
- The `PUT` route uses a numeric id (`%d`), matching `ApiService.update(endpoint, id, body)`.
- Design-language precedents for inline rename: `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` (inline input, Enter/Escape via `KeyManager`, autofocus) and `CreateEntry.svelte` (same key handling in the settings section). `DeleteButton` `minimal` style is used for the category pill actions.

